Hi Mark,
Just to clarify from the BiCoE side, our expectation was always that the Production Count file would continue in .csv format.
The .txt behaviour was identified in the lower environment after the AZ and Britannia files were merged. We specifically raised this in the group discussion to make sure the same behaviour did not reach Production. The conclusion from that discussion was that the Count file would continue as .csv after the merge.
We also understood that the merged-file change was planned for the 15 October Production release, following validation in the lower environment. Therefore, seeing a .txt Count file in the Production SFTP before that date was unexpected and is why we raised it.
Based on Sophie’s explanation, we now understand that this happened as part of the DR activity, where the UK West MoveIT job picked up the matched files.
There is also a separate reconciliation issue from the DR rollback activity. Two daily files were subsequently loaded into SFTP, whereas the BiCoE reconciliation process expects a single incremental file per day. As a result, only one of those files was processed and the other day was missed from reconciliation.
